raw:
{
  "ticket_text": "We’ve been locked out of our Northbeam account for over 45 minutes now — this is the second time this week that our finance team has been blocked from accessing the platform. Last week, we had a similar issue where we couldn’t access dashboards during the end-of-month close, and we had to manually log in from a backup workstation. This time, after multiple password reset attempts, we’re still unable to get in. We’re now unable to reconcile transactions, and our CFO has already called IT to verify if this is a system-wide outage. We’re worried this might be a repeat of last month’s incident where you initially said it was a user-level access issue but then confirmed it was a broader service failure. We need immediate help to regain access — we can’t work without it, and the month-end audit is due in 15 minutes. Our team is on hold, and we’re losing visibility into our P&Ls and expenses. Can you confirm whether this is a known account access issue or if there’s a service outage affecting all users? We’ve already tried resetting the password via email and using recovery options — nothing works. We need full access restored immediately.",
  "category": "account_access",
  "priority": "P2",
  "rationale": "A single user cannot get into their account: forgotten password loops, 2FA device lost, SSO misconfigured for one person, locked out after failed attempts, email change requests."
}

{
  "ticket_text": "We’ve been asking for a way to export financial summaries directly into Excel for months now. Last quarter, when we tried to export the revenue report, it just returned a blank file and we had to manually recompile everything — that took two full days. Our CFO is already frustrated because she can’t present accurate numbers at the monthly review. We’ve also had three separate incidents where the export function failed during peak reporting periods, and each time we were told it was a 'temporary technical issue' with no resolution. We’ve even reached out to support before, and the last time we were told the feature was 'on the roadmap' but still not available. We’re not asking for a minor tweak — we need a reliable, automated export of consolidated financial data so we can close our books on time. This isn’t just a small request; it’s been blocking our ability to meet deadlines and maintain financial integrity. Can we finally get this feature implemented so we’re not constantly fighting the system during critical periods?",
  "category": "feature_request",
  "priority": "P4",
  "rationale": "All feature_request tickets are categorized as P4, regardless of urgency or phrasing."
}

{
  "ticket_text": "I've been locked out of my account for three days now, and I can't even reset my password because the 2FA device I lost last month is the only one I have. I remember this happened last April too—after a similar device loss, and you told me it would take 24 hours to reset. This time, it's been three days and I haven't been able to get back in. My team is relying on me to approve invoices, and without access, I can't do anything. I feel like you're not taking this seriously because I’ve had to reach out multiple times before, and every time, the response was 'we’ll look into it'—but nothing actually changes. I’m not just asking for a password reset; I need a full 2FA recovery option or a temporary admin override so I can get back into the system. If I don’t get access in the next 12 hours, I’m going to have to notify my clients that the platform is down, which could damage our credibility. This is not just a small issue—it’s impacting business operations, and I’ve had to deal with this before, and it always takes way too long to resolve.",
  "category": "account_access",
  "priority": "P2",
  "rationale": "A single user cannot get into their account due to a lost 2FA device, and the customer is locked out, which falls under account_access/P2 as defined in the policy, unless it involves a suspected breach."
}
